From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-local <meta-local@local>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: always apply 128K SPL offset for U-Boot proper

Orange Pi 3 GPT images install u-boot-sunxi-with-spl.bin at 128 KiB so
the blob does not collide with the GPT partition-entry array at LBA
2..33. The H6 BROM loads that SPL, but boot_media does not always have
the HIGH bit set. In that case stock U-Boot looks for U-Boot proper at
the legacy 40 KiB sector and hangs at "Trying to boot from MMC1".

Always add the high-location sector fixup so U-Boot proper is read from
160 KiB (128 KiB SPL base + 32 KiB SPL pad), matching the on-disk layout.

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
@@ -346,12 +346,12 @@ unsigned long board_spl_mmc_get_uboot_raw_sector(struct mmc *mmc,
 
 	sector = max(raw_sect, spl_size / 512);
 
-	switch (sunxi_get_boot_source()) {
-	case SUNXI_BOOTED_FROM_MMC0_HIGH:
-	case SUNXI_BOOTED_FROM_MMC2_HIGH:
-		sector += (128 - 8) * 2;
-		break;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * GPT SD/eMMC images place the combined firmware at 128 KiB.
+	 * Always apply the high-location offset; do not rely on the BROM
+	 * HIGH bit in boot_media (often clear on H6).
+	 */
+	sector += (128 - 8) * 2;
 
 	return sector;
 }
